  "body": "# Desktop Pet v0.4.1 release notes\n\n## Publication boundary\n\nThis separately approved version preserves incoming Herdr plugin-manager work without replacing published neutral v0.4.0. **v0.4.1 is not yet published.** No release ID, clean-tagged archive digest or public installer result is claimed here. Published v0.4.0 and historical Herdr tags/assets remain immutable. Bridge and integration publication, the final migration matrix and account-dependent two-host acceptance remain separate.\n\n## Ownership and behavior\n\n- Herdr owns the optional manager UI, four-locale text, authenticated selected-host inventory, protected plugin roots, confirmation and guarded durable host mutations. Its original host patch stays in the Herdr integration repository; installing an integration never patches or replaces a host.\n- Core owns host-neutral preference access, bounded control transport, CAS and exact-operation uncertainty, offline ownership admission and shared lifecycle/profile persistence. Contracts retain a config-scoped preferences-owner FD, bound to the canonical config/state pair. A second state selection cannot write the same live config.\n- Install/Remove change only optional-component availability. Open explicitly discovers the selected host. No uncertain mutation replay, alternate-host/CLI fallback or fabricated completion is permitted. Operation lifetime descriptors remain distinct from short admission descriptors.\n- Native manager windows use readable dark appearance and the same floating level as Settings so the owning action can present them above Settings. Short manager admission explicitly unlocks on drop; it cannot be retained until exec by an unrelated fork. Long operation admission is intentionally not unlocked by that drop.\n\nDependency sources: contracts `85c644cd90d8c6a9e97e9dc313cc4750f344235f`, final Herdr adapter `fb28be4477b9a529e046a0f033ad9e2cd888abea`, Tern adapter `0c1b6ca173e9b31f191f92fa394a5a2429f7c099`. Native smoke below used Herdr `bf7a2cad6db59809fb418b0fa4e19f252ca49bc5`; the final adapter removes only an unused accessor and unused localized message. Incoming Herdr history was merged without force push; common application ownership was not restored to Herdr.\n\n## Observed pre-publication checks\n\nCommon contracts/core passed 652 tests. The final composed workspace passed **737**, including the actual AppKit composer path; **62 Bun tests** and TypeScript passed. Herdr adapter passed **105** after the presentation/admission correction and again after dead-code removal; Tern adapter passed **38**. The previously failing relative/alias manager-admission test passed after explicit short-lock release. A common owner-alias test also exposed same-clock-tick fixture-name collisions; atomic per-process fixture ordinals fixed isolation, and that targeted test plus the complete workspace passed. A final clean-source/tagged build remains required before publication. Tern has no Bun test suite; its actual supported-window transition harness remains blocked on the real window's sign-in/keychain prerequisite.\n\nReal disposable Mac runtime, not a mocked provider or receipt:\n\n- Published v0.4.0 allowed same config with different state (primary PID 1973, secondary PID 2579); the owned secondary was explicitly stopped. The v0.4.1 working-tree candidate rejected that scenario before writing: `another preferences writer owns this config profile`. Every config-file SHA remained identical and the original candidate primary PID 2740 / instance `fd9f26cdc5ee75c4479f9f6a4a87417c` stayed ready.\n- Corrected signed candidate: PID **3135**, instance **806a8f9d383fbb4469bf5097a89d4a2e**, image SHA-256 **8d780024730f12661a5505f73b44e77789011c820b89664b6d8280427fac1e40**; actual UI/control ready, Auto, Herdr 1 / Tern 0, matched 4/2/1 capabilities. This is a working-tree smoke image, not a published release archive.\n- An isolated real patched Herdr 0.9.3 server reported PID **2832**, protocol 2, manager safety 1, durable-result 1 and admission-FD 1. CLI context with wrong XDG roots failed closed; matching roots returned the actual socket/host/config/state. No installed host was replaced.\n- Actual native Install persisted `plugin_manager_installed:true`; actual Open showed authenticated inventory. The initial low-contrast/Settings-obscured window was observed before correction; corrected window was visually read above Settings with readable text.\n- The original host's `example.smoke` production fixture was linked only in that private server. Actual native confirmation and host execution completed Disable, Enable and Unlink; actual registry states matched each result. Local-source Update/Delete were visibly disabled. Unlink removed registration only and preserved the original manifest SHA-256 `1e984e502d6e6ab4e633594e6fd5e310161c887d39e2e592d386828884bd447a`.\n- Native availability Remove required its own confirmation, committed `plugin_manager_installed:false`, retained all three completed operation result files, and left the same PID 3135 / instance ready with Herdr connected. Removal is not plugin uninstall or evidence cleanup.\n\n| Action | Actual durable operation ID | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Disable | `4d4e93e80f3325ee7591b668420c7de37e6bc909cb0e6a7ca83f23193d6bc855` | `completed`; registry disabled |\n| Enable | `bc450b6a37e351de4ef6ad957ef6230c60ce92915632991afbb933249f924098` | `completed`; registry enabled |\n| Unlink | `ea5b41da7f015e99fd10808b208bff41c4a892d9113d5eed70aba0067d021a71` | `completed`; no registration; measured source bytes preserved |\n\nEvidence lives in the retained disposable `desktop-pet-public-brew` VM under `/Users/admin/desktop-pet-041-manager-owner-smoke`; host captures include `manager-041-durable-runtime-results.json` and the consent/result/settings PNGs in the private VM artifacts directory. This exercise does not establish managed Update/Uninstall execution, real two-host prompts/transcripts, official signing/notarization, Windows runtime or final public migration acceptance.\n"
}
